"# MP-AIIM-PROTO-BW-1.0 — Master Prompt and Subsequent Prompts\n\n**Purpose.** These prompts produce, and then upgrade, the TBCA AIIM Botswana prototype (web pages): a country cockpit, a drill-down country map and the nine AIIM sub-sections, with every word and cell of the Botswana Country Pack (BW-1.0, .docx) and the Botswana Deep Registers (BW-1.0, .xlsx) carried into it, and every embedded service in Batch 4D (581 rows) placed as a paid call to action. The prototype is the template for the 54-country rollout (CPDS-1.2).\n\n**Inputs.** (1) `TBCA_AIIM_Botswana_Country_Pack_BW-1.0.docx`. (2) `TBCA_AIIM_Botswana_Deep_Registers_BW-1.0.xlsx` (62 sheets). (3) `TBCA_Batch_4D_581_Embedded_Sprint_Workbook_REPRICED_v3.xlsx`. (4) The mock-up pages (Google Drive folder, Pages 1–82). (5) The live reference page `tbca.laravel.cloud/aiim/country/south-africa` (map component, colour tokens, cockpit layout).\n\n---\n\n## MASTER PROMPT (copy as one block)\n\nROLE. You are the TBCA AIIM Chief Product Designer, Information Architect and Front-end Engineer. You build investor-grade intelligence products to the standard of the best institutional data platforms, in TBCA's house style.\n\nOBJECTIVE. Build the Botswana AIIM prototype as a multi-page web application that (a) reproduces every mock-up page in the Drive folder in TBCA's style and improves on it, (b) absorbs 100 % of the Country Pack and the Deep Registers with nothing dropped, and (c) monetises every page through the Batch 4D embedded services.\n\nSTRUCTURE. Global header (brand, search, language EN/Setswana, currency BWP/USD/ZAR, Ask a Question, Start a Sprint, WhatsApp/Talk, Client Portal). AIIM sub-navigation in this order: Map View · Investor Info Type · Trader Info Type · Opportunities · Investors · Funders · Trade Corridors · Commodity HS · Risk & Outlook. Then the Botswana Investor Cockpit, the 18 sector pages, the 16 unit profiles, 83 town profiles, the opportunity, project, investor and funder previews, the premium brief store, the full commercial journey (Pages 19–82) and a Data Room that renders every register sheet.\n\nMAP. Show only Botswana when Botswana is selected (Africa appears only on the landing page). Drill: Country (L0) → Gateway region → District / City / Town council (L1) → Sub-district (L2, flagged DG-13) → Town or place (L3) → Site / hotspot (L4) → Lead and asset (L5). Layers: districts choropleth with a metric switch, 83 towns, 42 hotspots and 126 hotspot leads, 2,137 ranked leads, 10,346 coverage rows by sector, 6 border gateways, corridor lines, roads, rail, rivers, lakes, airports and the sector map stack. Use pins, lines, cards, charts, alerts and illumination (glow on Tier A+ and live leads). Every click opens an information card with the evidence ID, grade, freshness and the institution to call.\n\nDATA RULES. Use only the three files. Keep fact IDs, grades, dates and [VERIFY] / [PROPOSED] / [COMPUTED] markers visible. Never invent a number; where a figure is computed in the browser (counts, sums, shares), label it as computed. Show conflicts and open data gaps where they bear on a figure.\n\nCOMMERCE. On every page, place the matching embedded services with tier, entry price (ZAR, VAT-exclusive, shown in BWP/USD on switch), delivery time and automation level. Every opportunity, unit, town, sector, corridor and product carries a brief call to action routed to the premium store and the checkout flow.\n\nDESIGN. Corporate and elegant: TBCA near-black and gold with Botswana sky blue; cards, KPI tiles, charts drawn to scale, light and dark themes, phone width supported, keyboard accessible.\n\nQUALITY. Run a coverage check that counts every docx block and every sheet cell into the build. Run a render check. Publish, then report what was built, what is honest about the limits, and the next step.\n\nOUTPUTS. (1) This prompt pack. (2) The published prototype. (3) A coverage report.\n\n---\n\n## SUBSEQUENT PROMPTS\n\n| Prompt | Name | Task | Acceptance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P0 | Challenge | Review the mock-ups and the live SA page; list what the Botswana build must improve | ≥10 improvements named |\n| P1 | Ingest | Parse the docx into ordered blocks (headings, paragraphs, lists, tables) and all 62 sheets into column-packed JSON | Block count and cell count logged |\n| P2 | Geometry | Build Botswana layers (15 base polygons, Chobe as a flagged point, neighbours, roads, rail, rivers, lakes, airports) and the Africa layer for the landing page from public-domain Natural Earth | Map renders offline |\n| P3 | Shell | Header, AIIM sub-nav, router, currency and language switches, theme tokens, toasts, drawer | All 9 sub-sections routable |\n| P4 | Landing (Page 1) | Africa map with the 8 issued packs and the rollout waves; Botswana as the live cockpit | Clicking Botswana opens the cockpit |\n| P5 | Cockpit (Page 2) | KPIs from BW_Summary, unit heat list, top sectors, top units, risk snapshot, quick actions, CTA | Every tile traceable to a sheet |\n| P6 | Map View | Drill-down map with layers, metric switch, filters (sector, tier, persona, citizen, FX), search, info cards, alerts ticker | L0→L5 drill works |\n| P7 | Units (Pages 3–4) | 16-unit selector and unit profiles: population, places, templates, Tier A, envelopes, tags, towns, leads | 16/16 profiles |\n| P8 | Towns | 83 town profiles: gateway distance, hotspots, ranked leads, coverage by sector | 83/83 profiles |\n| P9 | Sectors (Pages 5–6, 54) | 18 sector pages with the full worked example, facts, chains, map stack, sweep, products, shocks | 18/18 sectors |\n| P10 | Investor Info Type | IQ01–IQ45 chain plus 18,810 BW rows and 4,600 Issue 2.0 rows, filterable by sector, asset and question | All rows reachable |\n| P11 | Trader Info Type | TQ01–TQ40 chain plus 5,600 BW rows and 3,523 Issue 2.0 rows | All rows reachable |\n| P12 | Opportunities (Pages 7–8) | 321-template sweep, priority list, 610 opportunities, 744 Issue 2.0 register rows, 190 worked-example rows, previews with brief CTA | Every Opp ID opens |\n| P13 | Projects (Pages 9–10) | 42 hotspots and 18 precedent deals as projects | Every project opens |\n| P14 | Investors (Pages 11–12) | Personas, strategic investors from precedents, capital pools, institutions | Persona top-5 lists shown |\n| P15 | Funders (Pages 13–14) | Development finance, pensions, capital markets, climate funds, envelopes | Unit envelopes charted |\n| P16 | Trade Corridors (Pages 15–16) | Gateways, corridor lines, catchments, TRN facts, trader chain | 6 gateways mapped |\n| P17 | Commodity HS | 55 Botswana products (English/Setswana) and 85 Issue 2.0 commodities with trader info types | Every HS code opens |\n| P18 | Risk & Outlook (Page 17) | Macro, benchmark, shocks matrix, downturn re-tiering, FX scenarios, regulatory change, conflicts, gaps, freshness | All registers shown |\n| P19 | Leads | Top 30, persona lists, hotspot leads, ranked leads, coverage, envelopes, concentration test | Counts match BW_Summary |\n| P20 | Economics | Unit economics, tornado, equity IRR, FX, precedents, time to revenue | 14 packs charted |\n| P21 | Evidence (Page 18, 82) | Facts, sources, verification log, validator, CPDS, conflicts | 102 + 27 facts |\n| P22 | Premium (Pages 34–38) | BW-PB-01…17 and the AIIM brief services with prices | Each has a buy path |\n| P23 | Commerce flow (Pages 19–33) | Registration, saved, watchlist, comparison, fees, manifest, locked object, metered unlock, wallet, checkout, payment, confirmation, entitlement | Flow runs end to end |\n| P24 | Advisory flow (Pages 39–53) | Custom intelligence, advisor request, discovery, quotation, engagement letter, e-signature, deposit, verification scope, cost approval, verification progress and report | Flow runs end to end |\n| P25 | Deal flow (Pages 54–64) | Deep dive, packaging, introduction consent and room, DD, VDR and Project Advisory hand-offs, delivery acceptance, scope change | Flow runs end to end |\n| P26 | After-sale (Pages 65–71) | Refund, dispute, pause, restart, cancellation, ledger | Each case page works |\n| P27 | Desks and admin (Pages 72–82) | Enterprise, API and white label, Government and DFI desk, monitoring alerts, archive, client, advisor, finance and admin dashboards, pricing and source administration | Each page renders Botswana data |\n| P28 | Services | All 581 embedded services by module, with the 162 AIIM services placed in context | 581/581 listed |\n| P29 | Country Pack and Data Room | Render the docx in full with a contents list; render all 62 sheets with search, sort and paging | 100 % coverage |\n| P30 | Coverage and QA | Count blocks and cells delivered vs source; render check at desktop and phone width, light and dark | 100 % and no overflow |\n| P31 | Publish and replicate | Publish; document the CPDS-1.2 swap-in for the next country (Namibia, Zambia, Zimbabwe first) | Link delivered |\n\n---\n\n## REPLICATION NOTE (54 countries)\n\nEvery page reads from the same sheet names (BW_* → XX_*). To build the next country, replace the three input files, rebuild the geometry for that ISO3 code and re-run P1–P31. Country-specific text lives only in the data, never in the page code.\n"